From 817d57f28c8a5dd4dfbbaf25d38b09c1714f16d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Revulate <76570121+Revulate@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Jun 2026 18:59:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] gpui: add Window::present_statistics for Echo metrics
 overlay

Expose swap-chain present timing so Echo's in-app metrics overlay can show
real present (vsync) latency instead of a stubbed "n/a".

On Windows, DirectXRenderer::present_statistics maps
IDXGISwapChain::GetFrameStatistics (the swap chain is flip-model:
DXGI_SWAP_EFFECT_FLIP_SEQUENTIAL) plus the high-resolution performance
counter into a small PresentStatistics { present_count, present_latency_ms }.
present_latency_ms is the age of the most recently scanned-out frame
(now QPC - SyncQPCTime). Returns None when statistics are unavailable, when
DXGI reports them transiently disjoint, or before the first vsync-aligned
present -- never fabricated. The PlatformWindow trait method defaults to None,
so macOS/Linux/test backends are unaffected. GPU timestamp queries remain out
of scope (no query-heap pipeline).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
